{"abstract":[{"text":"Remote request verification.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Http security","modules":[{"name":"Vernissage"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vernissage authenticates every ActivityPub request with exactly the same HTTP Signature scheme that Mastodon describes in its security specification. Each inbound request must include a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Signature"},{"type":"text","text":" header that:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"points to the sender’s public key with keyId,"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"lists the headers that were signed (commonly (request-target) host date digest), and","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"contains a Base-64-encoded RSA-SHA256 signature of those header values.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When Vernissage receives the request it reconstructs the signed string, fetches the public key referenced by keyId, and verifies the signature. For POST requests it additionally checks the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Digest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header against the body and rejects any message whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header is older than 12 hours, ensuring both authenticity and integrity of the message.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See the full description in Mastodon’s documentation: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.joinmastodon.org\/spec\/security\/#http"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/VernissageServer\/documentation\/VernissageServer\/HttpSecurity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"